<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dobromir Chrysos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1185–1202</span> · Also known as Dobromir Hriz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dobromir Chrysos was a Vlach or Bulgarian commander who served in the Byzantine army and broke away during the Asen revolt that created the Second Bulgarian Empire. From the fortress of Prosek in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vardar">Vardar</a> gorge he ruled an independent lordship in Macedonia, fought off Byzantine attacks and was recognised by Emperor Alexios III, before losing his lands around 1202.</p></div>
